I happen to think you're wrong, but that is neither here nor there.

Allowing nonnormative usage is good, because for some people certain
nonnormative styles are easier. For example, SOV is more natural (to me)
than making something special about the x1 place - I prefer "mi le zarci cu
klama" to "mi klama le zarci", though with long sumti my selbri tend to
float around a lot.

As for /y'y/ as [@T@], some of us feel this is better. Criticizing us when
your only reason is "you don't have a reason to do it your way" (which is
just plain false) is both unnecessary and divisive.





           

